title The grammar and three readings
prompt Keaton: kg on laps C through H -- and mid-round, the sharper form of lap H: are there context files that should be molt-breached into foundations, or the reverse, with renamings and fascia repointing allowed.
think Lap E writes a grammar. CONTRIBUTING gains nine bracket classes for pull request titles, each pointing at the law it answers to, and three body shapes written out ready to fill -- foundations harmony, rota adherence, active-designing progression, the three Keaton named.
think The bracket rides OUTSIDE the fifty-character subject budget, so Urbit's inherited rule is untouched and the class costs nothing. One class per title; work spanning two is usually two pull requests.
think Depersonalization falls out of the shape rather than being asked for. A pull request names its LANE, the lane is a row in the one seat table, and between what changed and where it belongs there is nowhere a person is needed.
think Laps F, G and H each ask a question rather than name a repair, so each closes with a number and a verdict rather than a diff.
obs LAP B IS WHAT MADE LAP F MEASURABLE. external-research links into gratitude from 109 files across 14 targets; 11 resolve in the field and 10 now resolve in the SEED, which none could before the room was allowed in. The eleventh is a gitlink, withheld by licence, and that earns a small rule: cite the thanks page, never the gitlink directory. Zero living files reach past it.
obs THE SILO READS 29 OF 33, AND THE FOUR EXCEPTIONS ARE REALLY ONE. Deriving the teacher names from the gratitude room's own person-shaped filenames, fifteen of forty appear in foundations and active-designing across 33 mentions; 29 carry a gratitude pointer. Two of the four bare ones name OUR OWN whitepaper, one is an index row, and one is a dated study. Nothing living to repair, and the practice reads stronger than the law had been asked to prove.
obs I DECLINED THE MOVE KEATON GRANTED, AND THE DECLINE IS THE MEASUREMENT. Three tells agree the two rooms are already separate: context holds 28 files and ZERO carry a stamp; foundations holds 84 and 81 do; the eleven foundations cited by rules are cited as canon, which is the design rather than a misfile; and of the fourteen context files no rule cites, all fourteen read normative. APARIGRAHA was the one candidate and it carries Status Living pin with four named budgets. Duplicating a hundred pages into a second room would be a second COPY, which is the fault alias-sameness exists to prevent.
obs THE ONE THING WORTH DOING WAS RECORDING RATHER THAN MOVING. The two unstamped universals in foundations carry their exception only in their own Status lines, so a first-time reader re-derives it. Named at the room's front door now, with the two counts beside it.
obs THE SEED GUARD CAUGHT MY OWN PROSE POINTING AT A ROOM IT CANNOT SEE. Both new sections linked construction/fleet-roster.kyri, and construction is personal -- the seed never carries it -- so seed_link rose 848 to 850 and refused. The room is NAMED in prose now rather than linked, which is the scan's own advice, and both pages say why the link is absent so a maintainer reading the field copy is not confused by its absence.
obs A PEER'S BROKEN LINK REDDENED THREE GUARDS ON MY LAP. construction/ITINERARY.md cited archive/REDS-...-rows-492.md while the shelf on disk reads rows-494 -- readme_reach, reds_fold and seed_link all refused, and only the first names the file. Repaired here rather than handed back: a red found is a red repaired, and the number in a shelf name is the row it holds.
